Pagination bug reported: every page is missing its last row. Save /workspace/paginate.mjs:

export function paginate(items, page, perPage) {
  const start = page * perPage;
  return items.slice(start, start + perPage - 1);
}
// page is documented as 1-based: paginate(items, 1, 10) is the first ten items.

Two bugs: the slice end drops one element, and the 1-based contract is ignored (page 1 actually skips the first perPage items). Write paginate.test.mjs with node:test first, covering: 25 items with perPage 10 gives pages of 10, 10, 5; page 1 starts at the first item; page beyond the end returns []; perPage 1 works. Run node --test, confirm the failures, fix the function, and finish with all tests passing plus an invariant test that concatenating all pages reconstructs the original array for a dozen random sizes.

tools_list = await mcp.list_tools("tools")
for t in tools_list:
    print(t["name"], t["inputSchema"])

